Hello everybody,

I
have three capital
cities
in my map (longitudes
and latitudes
of the points: Buenos
aires,
Paris
and Melbourne are provided below). I would like to draw arrows of
different colors and later show the points and arrows on the legend
of my map. One
arrow should move from Melbourne
to Paris
(this arrow can be red in color and named first). Another arrow drawn
from Paris
to Buenos
aires
(this arrow can be green in color and named second). The cities
in the map should
be named and
can be represented
by
different shapes ie rectangle, triangle etc. I would really appreciate any help on this.

Regards,

Dikko.

Buenos_aires=c(-58,-34)

Paris=c(2,49)

Melbourne=c(145,-38)

data=rbind(Buenos_aires,
Paris, Melbourne) %>% as.data.frame()

colnames(data)=c("long","lat")

points(x=data$long,
y=data$lat, col="slateblue", cex=3, pch=20)

##Read in the libararies

library(maptools)

library(rgdal)

library(rgeos)

library(sp)

library(ggplot2)

##get
the data

data("wrld_simpl")

crs(wrld_simpl)

plot(wrld_simpl)

##change
into a format that can be used in ggplot2

AG
<- fortify(wrld_simpl)

names(AG)

###plot
with ggplot2 package

ggplot()+
geom_polygon(data=AG, aes(long, lat, group = group), colour =
alpha("darkred", 1/2), size = 0.7, fill = 'skyblue', alpha
= .3)

